  doi = {10.1017/jfm.2013.39},
  urldate = {2022-02-24},
  abstract = {Abstract                            We investigate the problem of oscillatory flow of a homogeneous fluid with viscosity                                                                      \${\textbackslash}nu \$                                               in a fluid-filled sphere of radius                                                                      \$a\$                                               that rotates rapidly about a fixed axis with angular velocity                                                                      \$\{{\textbackslash}Omega \}\_\{0\} \$                                               and that undergoes weak longitudinal libration with amplitude                                                                      \${\textbackslash}epsilon \{{\textbackslash}Omega \}\_\{0\} \$                                               and frequency                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \{{\textbackslash}Omega \}\_\{0\} \$                                               , where                                                                      \${\textbackslash}epsilon \$                                               is the Poincar{\'e} number with                                                                      \${\textbackslash}epsilon {\textbackslash}ll 1\$                                               and                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               is dimensionless frequency with                                                                      \$0{\textbackslash}lt {\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} {\textbackslash}lt 2\$                                               . Three different methods are employed in this investigation: (i) asymptotic analysis at small Ekman numbers                                                                      \$E\$                                               defined as                                                                      \$E= {\textbackslash}nu / (\{a\}{\textasciicircum}\{2\} \{{\textbackslash}Omega \}\_\{0\} )\$                                               ; (ii) linear numerical analysis using a spectral method; and (iii) nonlinear direct numerical simulation using a finite-element method. A satisfactory agreement among the three different sets of solutions is achieved when                                                                      \$E{\textbackslash}leq 1\{0\}{\textasciicircum}\{- 4\} \$                                               . It is shown that the flow amplitude                                                                      \${\textbackslash}vert {\textbackslash}boldsymbol\{u\}{\textbackslash}vert \$                                               is nearly independent of both the Ekman number                                                                      \$E\$                                               and the libration frequency                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               , always obeying the asymptotic scaling                                                                      \${\textbackslash}vert {\textbackslash}boldsymbol\{u\}{\textbackslash}vert = O({\textbackslash}epsilon )\$                                               even though various spherical inertial modes are excited by longitudinal libration at different libration frequencies                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               . Consequently, resonances do not occur in this system even when                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               is at the characteristic value of an inertial mode. It is also shown that the pressure difference along the axis of rotation is anomalous: this quantity reaches a sharp peak when                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               approaches a characteristic value. In contrast, the pressure difference measured at other places in the sphere, such as in the equatorial plane, and the volume-integrated kinetic energy are nearly independent of both the Ekman number                                                                      \$E\$                                               and the libration frequency                                                                      \${\textbackslash}hat \{{\textbackslash}omega \} \$                                               . Absence of resonances in a fluid-filled sphere forced by longitudinal libration is explained through the special properties of the analytical solution that satisfies the no-slip boundary condition and is valid for                                                                      \$E{\textbackslash}ll 1\$                                               and                                                                      \${\textbackslash}epsilon {\textbackslash}ll 1\$                                               .},
  langid = {english},
